<Post slug="how-often-should-a-business-be-cleaned" faqs={faqs}>
  <p>Clean too little and your space looks tired, restrooms run out of supplies and customers notice. Clean too often and you pay for work you do not need. The right frequency depends on how many people use your space, what kind of business you run and what your customers expect. Here is a practical way to decide.</p>

  <h2>Start with traffic, not square footage</h2>
  <p>Size tells you how long a visit takes. Traffic tells you how often you need one. A 3,000 sq ft office with six people and few visitors stays clean much longer than a 3,000 sq ft office with thirty desks, a busy kitchen and clients coming in all day. Before choosing a frequency, think about:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>How many people are in the space each day, including customers or patients</li>
    <li>How many restrooms there are and how heavily they are used</li>
    <li>Whether people eat on site, and how busy the kitchen or break room is</li>
    <li>How much sand, rain and dirt comes in from outside (in Southwest Florida, usually a lot)</li>
    <li>Whether customers judge your business by how it looks</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Common choices by type of business</h2>
  <h3>Offices</h3>
  <p>Small offices with a few people often do well with one or two visits a week. Mid-size offices with a shared kitchen and regular client visits usually choose three. Large or very busy offices often need five. See our <a href="/services/office-cleaning">office cleaning</a> page for what each visit includes.</p>
  <h3>Medical and dental offices</h3>
  <p>Patients expect a clean office every day it is open, and restrooms and waiting rooms get heavy use. Most practices choose three to five visits a week, usually after the last patient. Learn more about <a href="/services/medical-office-cleaning">medical office cleaning</a>.</p>
  <h3>Retail stores and showrooms</h3>
  <p>Stores with steady foot traffic usually need at least two or three visits a week to keep floors and glass looking good. Showrooms with fewer visitors may do fine with one. Read about <a href="/services/retail-showroom-cleaning">retail and showroom cleaning</a>.</p>
  <h3>Gyms and fitness studios</h3>
  <p>Locker rooms and showers get dirty fast. Gyms open long hours usually need five visits a week; smaller studios may choose two or three. See <a href="/services/gym-fitness-cleaning">gym and fitness cleaning</a>.</p>
  <h3>Warehouses and light industrial spaces</h3>
  <p>The offices, restrooms and break rooms often need cleaning two or three times a week, while the open floor may only need sweeping once or twice a week. See <a href="/services/warehouse-industrial-cleaning">warehouse and industrial cleaning</a>.</p>

  <h2>What the frequency options mean</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Monthly:</strong> about one visit a month. Works for very low-use spaces, but each visit takes more work.</li>
    <li><strong>Every 2 weeks:</strong> about two visits a month. Good for small, quiet spaces.</li>
    <li><strong>1x per week:</strong> about four visits a month. A common choice for small offices and showrooms.</li>
    <li><strong>2x or 3x per week:</strong> about 9 or 13 visits a month. The most common choice for busy offices, stores and practices.</li>
    <li><strong>5x per week:</strong> about 22 visits a month. For medical offices, gyms and any space with heavy daily traffic.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How frequency changes the cost</h2>
  <p>Cleaning more often means each visit is a bit faster, because the space never gets very dirty. So the price per visit goes down as frequency goes up, while the monthly total goes up because there are more visits. Our <a href="/estimate">estimator</a> shows this directly: try the same space with different frequencies and compare. For more on pricing, read <a href="/blog/commercial-cleaning-cost-naples-fl">how much commercial cleaning costs in Naples</a>.</p>

  <h2>Signs you need more frequent cleaning</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Restrooms run out of supplies or look used by mid-day</li>
    <li>Trash bins are full before the next visit</li>
    <li>Floors show sand and footprints soon after cleaning</li>
    <li>Your team starts cleaning up themselves between visits</li>
    <li>Customers or patients comment on the space</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Plan for the season</h2>
  <p>Many businesses in <a href="/locations/naples">Naples</a>, <a href="/locations/bonita-springs">Bonita Springs</a>, <a href="/locations/estero">Estero</a> and <a href="/locations/marco-island">Marco Island</a> are busier in the winter and spring. A flexible plan lets you add visits when traffic is high and scale back in the summer.</p>

  <h2>Not sure? Ask during the walkthrough</h2>
  <p>During our free walkthrough we look at your space and traffic and recommend a frequency. You decide, and you can change it later.</p>
